<title>SWEDEN: Saab to hire 200 more-paper.</title>
<headline>Saab to hire 200 more-paper.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saab Automobile AB, jointly owned by Investor AB  and General Motors Corp, is to hire 200 more staff at its Trollhattan plant in western Sweden, the daily Goteborgs Posten reported on Monday.</p>
<p>Most of the new staff will be needed for final assembly but some also in the chassis and materials handling sections.</p>
<p>Personnel manager Jan Dahlman was quoted as saying the factory would introduce a second shift on the Saab 9000 production line next year.</p>
<p>The Saab 9000 and new Saab 640 will be assembled on the same line, while the Saab 900 will continue to be assembled separately, the paper said.</p>
<p>-- Henrik Alberius, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1250</p>
